---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../../../lib/site';
---
<Layout
  title="DigUp for Customer Support — Macros, Recodings &amp; Help PDFs"
  description="Support agents find macros, call recordings, and help-center PDFs by meaning with DigUp on-device EmbeddingGemma 2 search."
  canonicalPath="/guides/use-cases/customer-support/"
  lang="en"
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <p class="meta-line"><span class="badge">Use case</span> · Customer support</p>
      <h1>DigUp for customer support</h1>
      <p class="lead">Ticket tools search tickets; DigUp searches your local runbooks, screenshots, and call audio with EmbeddingGemma 2.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="wide">
      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.downloads.mac} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Download DigUp for Mac</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/embeddinggemma-2/">EmbeddingGemma 2</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href="/guides/use-cases/">All roles</a>
      </div>
      <figure class="shot-panel" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
        <span class="shot-label">On-device flow</span>
        <img src="/media/use-cases/customer-support.svg" width="960" height="540" alt="Schematic: DigUp uses EmbeddingGemma 2 for Customer support local search" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption class="shot-caption">Original schematic — DigUp indexes local files with EmbeddingGemma 2 (llama.cpp).</figcaption>
      </figure>
      
      <h2>Sourced snapshot (2026-10-15)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Fact</th><th>Value</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Model</td><td>EmbeddingGemma 2 · ~740M params · ~865 MB Q8 via llama.cpp</td><td><a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/embeddinggemma" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google AI</a> · DigUp README</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Vector space</td><td>768-d shared multimodal space</td><td>Google AI · DigUp README</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mac / Win·Linux</td><td>0.6.1 · 0.7.0-beta.2</td><td>GitHub Releases</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stars / forks</td><td>~3,768 / ~254</td><td>GitHub API</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <h2>Pain → DigUp workflow → tip</h2>
      <table><thead><tr><th>Pain</th><th>DigUp + EmbeddingGemma 2 workflow</th><th>Tip</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Which runbook covers refund edge case?</td><td>Index support PDFs/md</td><td>Semantic + keyword</td></tr><tr><td>Call where user described error UI</td><td>Audio windows</td><td>Jump near description</td></tr><tr><td>Screenshot of rare settings panel</td><td>Image (+ Mac OCR)</td><td>Find by panel contents</td></tr><tr><td>Agent laptop privacy</td><td>Local-first DigUp</td><td>No DigUp telemetry of file contents (README)</td></tr></tbody></table>
      <h2>Numbered checklist</h2>
      <ol class="checklist"><li>Install DigUp; index Knowledge / Recordings allowed by policy.</li><li>Finish EmbeddingGemma 2 download (~865 MB).</li><li>Search customer phrases, not only internal IDs.</li><li>Verify before pasting into replies.</li><li>See zero-files guide if synced knowledge base is cloud-only.</li></ol>
      <h2>Why EmbeddingGemma 2 matters here</h2>
      <p>Google’s <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemma/docs/embeddinggemma" rel="noopener noreferrer">EmbeddingGemma 2</a> (~740M, unified 768-d multimodal space) is what DigUp runs via llama.cpp (~865 MB Q8 package). One query can rank images, PDF pages, audio windows, video frames, and optional code — see the <a href="/guides/embeddinggemma-2-local-multimodal-search/">local multimodal guide</a> and <a href="/embeddinggemma-2/">model page</a>. digup.run is not Google-official.</p>
      <h2>Downloads &amp; installs</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><a href={SITE.downloads.mac} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Mac DMG {SITE.downloads.macVersion}</a> · <a href="/install-mac/">Mac install</a></li>
        <li><a href={SITE.downloads.windows} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Windows {SITE.downloads.windowsVersion}</a> · <a href="/install-windows/">Windows install</a></li>
        <li><a href={SITE.downloads.linuxDeb} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Linux .deb</a> / <a href={SITE.downloads.linuxAppImage} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>AppImage</a> · <a href="/install-linux/">Linux install</a></li>
        <li><a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> · <a href="/faq/#model-size">Model size / Use Files…</a></li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Related</h2>
      <div class="cards"><a class="card" href="/guides/use-cases/"><h3>All roles hub</h3><p>Browse every use case</p></a><a class="card" href="/embeddinggemma-2/"><h3>EmbeddingGemma 2</h3><p>Model size &amp; runtime</p></a><a class="card" href="/guides/embeddinggemma-2-local-multimodal-search/"><h3>Multimodal guide</h3><p>Photos · PDF · audio · video · code</p></a><a class="card" href="/guides/use-cases/developer/"><h3>Developers &amp; programmers</h3><p>Role playbook</p></a><a class="card" href="/guides/use-cases/office-clerk/"><h3>Office clerks &amp; admins</h3><p>Role playbook</p></a><a class="card" href="/guides/use-cases/accountant/"><h3>Finance &amp; accountants</h3><p>Role playbook</p></a></div>
      <div class="cta-bar">
        <a class="cta" href={SITE.downloads.mac} rel="noopener noreferrer" download>Download DigUp for Mac</a>
        <a class="cta-secondary" href={SITE.upstreamRepo} rel="noopener noreferrer">ARahim3/DigUp</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
